From 02eec2bac4d3d38ee35e9d7c0a91d3fabc90e14f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 15:14:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 19/23] UML-ANDROID-LOCAL: cuttlefish drop the Bluetooth audio
 policy include

The UML product omits the Bluetooth HAL, and the target-files policy forbids
shipping bluetooth_with_le_audio_policy_configuration_7_0.xml. The audio policy
configuration still XIncluded that fragment, and the failed include invalidated
the whole document rather than just the Bluetooth section:

  AHAL_Config: Invalid XML config file: /vendor/etc/audio_policy_configuration.xml
  AHAL_Config: getEngineConfig: No audio configuration files found
  AHAL_Config: number of strategies parsed: 0, default strategy: -1

With zero modules parsed the audio HAL never registered
android.hardware.audio.core.IModule/default, audioserver never published
IAudioPolicyService, system_server blocked in AudioService.<init>, and the
watchdog killed the system process every 69 s so sys.boot_completed never
became 1.

Remove the include instead of restoring the fragment, so the configuration
declares only the primary and remote-submix modules this product actually
provides.

Change-Id: Idcbd385e8b5eb19e10dc77434b5ec596a30ae2fb
---
 shared/config/audio/policy/audio_policy_configuration.xml | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/shared/config/audio/policy/audio_policy_configuration.xml b/shared/config/audio/policy/audio_policy_configuration.xml
index 3c07e675c8e1264d8b76e505dd3c39d0331a747f..07e3716c418535e4ad04ffc8efabed9ac27bc59c 100644
--- a/shared/config/audio/policy/audio_policy_configuration.xml
+++ b/shared/config/audio/policy/audio_policy_configuration.xml
@@ -27,8 +27,6 @@
         <!-- Remote Submix Audio HAL -->
         <xi:include href="r_submix_audio_policy_configuration.xml"/>
 
-        <!-- Bluetooth Audio HAL -->
-        <xi:include href="bluetooth_with_le_audio_policy_configuration_7_0.xml"/>
     </modules>
     <!-- End of Modules section -->
 
